### Validation Implementation
- Car LOB check: `$quoteTypeId == QuoteTypes::CAR->id()`
- Health LOB check: `$quoteTypeId == QuoteTypes::HEALTH->id()`
- Conditional field validation using `withValidator()` method
- Uses `filled()` method to check field presence
- Comprehensive logging of validation failures with `LoggerService`
- Custom error messages and attributes for user-friendly feedback

### Validation Patterns
- Plate number: `/^[A-Za-z0-9\-\s]+$/` (actual pattern from ClaimDetailsUpdateRequest)
- Name validation: `/^[a-zA-Z\s\'-\.]+$/` for first and last names
- Phone validation: `/^[\+]?[0-9\s\-\(\)]+$/` for mobile numbers
- Standard field trimming in `prepareForValidation()`
- Uppercase transformation for plate numbers
- Email normalization to lowercase

### ClaimStoreRequest Validation
- Required: first_name, last_name, mobile_no, email, quote_type_id, claim_type_id
- Optional: customer_id, insurance_provider_id, claim_number, policy_number, incident_date, incident_story
- Car fields: plate_number, car_make, car_model, model_year
- Health fields: claim_request_type_id, service_type_id, request_reference_number
- Financial fields: approved_repair_amount, approved_total_loss_amount, approved_cash_loss_amount

### ClaimDetailsUpdateRequest Validation
- Required: claim_number, incident_date (must be before today)
- Car-specific interdependent validation: if one car field (plate_number, car_make, car_model, model_year) is provided, all must be provided
- Health-specific: claim_request_type_id required, service_type_id required when claim_request_type_id is 'pending-approvals'
- Conditional validation based on LOB using `validateCarFields()` and `validateHealthFields()` methods in `withValidator()`
- Special handling for claim_decline_reason: triggers automatic claim closure when filled

### ClaimSendNotificationRequest Validation
- Required fields: `customer_message`, `ai_optimized_message`, `claim_sub_status_id`
- Sub-status validation: must exist in `claim_statuses` table with `status_type` = 'sub-statuses'
- Message validation: both customer and AI optimized messages required as strings

## Observer-Specific Business Logic

### ClaimRequestObserver Requirements
- Auto-set `sub_status` to `CLAIM_REGISTERED` or `CLAIM_REGISTERED_AWAITING_INSPECTION` (for Car LOB) on creation
- Monitor `claim_number` changes: auto-update sub-status when claim number is entered
- Monitor `claim_sub_status_id` changes for auto-closure triggers
- Monitor approval amounts: `approved_repair_amount`, `approved_total_loss_amount`, `approved_cash_loss_amount`
- Auto-update sub-statuses based on approval amounts for Car/Bike LOB
- Monitor `claim_status_id` changes for Google review email dispatch (currently commented out)
- Log all status transitions with user context using ClaimsService methods

### Monitored Fields for Business Rules
- `claim_number` - When changed from empty to filled, triggers sub-status update to "Claim registered" or "Claim registered and awaiting inspection" (Car LOB)
- `claim_sub_status_id` - Triggers closure logic based on LOB-specific closure states using `checkSubStatusForClaimClosure()`
- `approved_repair_amount` - Car/Bike LOB only: When changed from empty to filled, triggers "Repair approved & work in progress" status
- `approved_total_loss_amount` - Car/Bike LOB only: When changed from empty to filled, triggers "Total Loss Offer Letter shared" status
- `approved_cash_loss_amount` - Car/Bike LOB only: When changed from empty to filled, triggers "Cash loss approved" status
- `claim_status_id` - Prepared for Google review email dispatch via `dispatchGoogleReviewEmail()` (currently commented out in observer)

### Observer Business Logic Methods (from ClaimStatusesService)
- `updateClaimSubStatusToClaimRegistered(ClaimRequest $claim)` - Sets "Claims registered" for general or "Claim registered and awaiting inspection" for Car LOB
- `checkSubStatusForClaimClosure(ClaimRequest $claim, $newClaimSubStatusId)` - Returns bool; checks if new sub-status is in closure list for claim's LOB
- `markClaimAsClosed(ClaimRequest $claim)` - Updates claim_status_id to "Closed" status using updateQuietly
- `markClaimAsReOpen(ClaimRequest $claim)` - Updates claim_status_id to "Reopen" status when complaint opened
- `updateClaimSubStatus(ClaimRequest $claim, $claimStatus)` - Sets sub-status using saveQuietly to prevent observer loops
- `isClaimStatusClosed(?int $statusId)` - Checks if status ID matches "Closed" status text

### Observer Business Logic Methods (from ClaimsService)
- `updateClaimSubStatusToRepairApprovedAndWIP(ClaimRequest $claim)` - Sets "Repair approved & work in progress" status
- `updateClaimSubStatusToTotalLossOfferLetterShared(ClaimRequest $claim)` - Sets "Total Loss Offer Letter shared" status
- `updateClaimSubStatusToCashLossApproved(ClaimRequest $claim)` - Sets "Cash loss approved" status
- `dispatchGoogleReviewEmail(ClaimRequest $claim)` - Dispatches SendGoogleReviewEmailJob for closed claims

